   "text": "✗ **H_pherc1203_xz_lasagna_77kev_upper_z_zscore** · hypothesis\n\nCoupling S3 77keV normal-grids/xz+yz vertical sheet trajectories (dx/dz=-0.27..+0.38) with Lasagna v2 cos/nx/ny phase field in the untouched upper 60% of PHerc1203_77keV (z_HI_L2=1400..3300 / z_LO=9370..11320, where zero auto_grown segments exist) + Nieuwlaar 31-depth pooled Z-score & (40,200) tile-phase ensemble will eliminate the dz=20 wrap-hopping artifact (19 vox vs true 450 vox radial shift) and isolate >=1 single-sheet papyrus region with z_ens >= +2.2 sigma and depth drop >= 35% at d=+-4\n\n*why dead:* [L-VFLU-002=0] Option C (8/8 sheets in z_HI_L2=1250..3550 on A100) fixed the central sheet weave and lifted Nieuwlaar Z-score to +3.9..+5.5 sigma (drop 36.5..47.0%, Hecate drop up to 54.5%), but 1D-coupled xz/yz+xy tracking still crosses S-folds at patch margins and ink detections remain fragmentary blobs without naked-eye Greek letters (confirming Dr Paul Henderson review).",
